1
00:00:02,915 --> 00:00:04,265
[narrator]
Previously on
"The Mentalist.."

2
00:00:04,352 --> 00:00:05,657
You know what Red John's
trying to do, don't you?

3
00:00:05,744 --> 00:00:07,398
He asked me
if I'm ready to quit.

4
00:00:07,485 --> 00:00:10,140
- How does Jane seem to you?
- I think he's in trouble.

5
00:00:10,227 --> 00:00:11,924
You tortured the guy,
for Christ sakes.

6
00:00:12,012 --> 00:00:14,927
I gave an evil psychopath
justice.

7
00:00:15,015 --> 00:00:16,668
I'm not gonna apologize.

8
00:00:16,755 --> 00:00:18,757
You're fired.

9
00:00:18,844 --> 00:00:20,324
Get outta here right now.

10
00:00:20,411 --> 00:00:22,413
Don't do anything rash.
We can work this out.

11
00:00:22,500 --> 00:00:24,763
We'll fix it.

12
00:00:24,850 --> 00:00:26,113
Idoubt that.

13
00:00:26,200 --> 00:00:29,029
Let me help you.

14
00:00:31,074 --> 00:00:33,990
[instrumental music]

15
00:00:44,087 --> 00:00:47,003
[music continues]

16
00:00:58,232 --> 00:00:59,407
Hey, Sammy.

17
00:00:59,494 --> 00:01:00,886
Hey.

18
00:01:00,973 --> 00:01:04,586
- Thank you.
- There you go.

19
00:01:09,634 --> 00:01:10,766
[glass clatters]

20
00:01:12,811 --> 00:01:13,986
[exhales sharply]

21
00:01:18,861 --> 00:01:20,993
Magic, huh?

22
00:01:21,081 --> 00:01:22,125
"Magic?"

23
00:01:22,212 --> 00:01:23,561
Tough business.

24
00:01:23,648 --> 00:01:25,520
Yeah. No,
uh, I'm-I'm..

25
00:01:25,607 --> 00:01:26,912
...I'm not
a magician, no.

26
00:01:26,999 --> 00:01:29,132
- No?
- No.

27
00:01:29,219 --> 00:01:32,048
You do coin tricks
and you have the look.

28
00:01:32,135 --> 00:01:34,137
What is the look?

29
00:01:34,224 --> 00:01:36,444
Like you're hiding stuff.

30
00:01:36,531 --> 00:01:37,923
I've seen you around..

31
00:01:38,010 --> 00:01:39,751
Served you drinks
a couple times.

32
00:01:39,838 --> 00:01:40,883
Yeah, I remember.

33
00:01:40,970 --> 00:01:43,320
Uh, Lorelei, right?

34
00:01:43,407 --> 00:01:44,756
How you doing?
I'm-I'm Patrick.

35
00:01:44,843 --> 00:01:46,062
Hey, Patrick.

36
00:01:46,149 --> 00:01:48,543
So you're not a magician?

37
00:01:48,630 --> 00:01:50,414
No. No,
I'm a con man.

38
00:01:50,501 --> 00:01:52,938
I steal from people.

39
00:01:53,025 --> 00:01:55,506
Ah, wow!

40
00:01:55,593 --> 00:01:57,465
You just come
right out and say it.

41
00:01:57,552 --> 00:02:00,468
"I steal from people"
like, "I sell shoes"

42
00:02:00,555 --> 00:02:01,599
like, it's not
a big deal.

43
00:02:01,686 --> 00:02:02,818
Well, it's not
a big deal.

44
00:02:02,905 --> 00:02:03,819
If you know
what you're doing

45
00:02:03,906 --> 00:02:05,821
it's very easy.

46
00:02:05,908 --> 00:02:07,649
Well, it's a big deal
because it's wrong

47
00:02:07,736 --> 00:02:09,868
to steal from people.

48
00:02:09,955 --> 00:02:11,566
No such thing as wrong.

49
00:02:11,653 --> 00:02:13,742
Really?
When did that happen?

50
00:02:13,829 --> 00:02:17,006
Well, there's
legal or illegal.

51
00:02:17,093 --> 00:02:20,052
There's, uh...happy or sad.

52
00:02:20,140 --> 00:02:24,100
Rich or poor,
alive or...dead.

53
00:02:24,187 --> 00:02:26,407
But there's
no wrong or right.

54
00:02:26,494 --> 00:02:28,800
Stuff just happens,
that's all.

55
00:02:28,887 --> 00:02:30,324
One damn thing
after another.

56
00:02:30,411 --> 00:02:32,500
Of course,there's wrong or right.

57
00:02:32,587 --> 00:02:35,633
You know that.

58
00:02:36,765 --> 00:02:39,246
I killed a man last year.

59
00:02:39,333 --> 00:02:41,465
Turns out he wasn't
the man I wanted to kill.

60
00:02:41,552 --> 00:02:43,989
Wrong guy. Anyway..

61
00:02:44,076 --> 00:02:45,295
..now when I recall

62
00:02:45,382 --> 00:02:48,385
shooting him dead..

63
00:02:48,472 --> 00:02:51,127
...still feels good.

64
00:02:51,214 --> 00:02:53,782
It's a happy
little memory to cherish..

65
00:02:53,869 --> 00:02:56,045
...like Christmas.

66
00:02:56,132 --> 00:02:58,961
Now you're just trying
to shock me, aren't you?

67
00:02:59,048 --> 00:03:00,832
- Yes.
- Mm-hmm.

68
00:03:00,919 --> 00:03:02,573
You seem
like a happy soul, Lorelei.

69
00:03:02,660 --> 00:03:05,141
- You happy?
- Yes. I am.

70
00:03:05,228 --> 00:03:07,143
- Well, that's nice.
- Mm-hmm.

71
00:03:07,230 --> 00:03:10,015
What's your secret?

72
00:03:10,102 --> 00:03:13,715
- Faith.
- Oh...yes.

73
00:03:13,802 --> 00:03:15,282
Yes, I've heard that.

74
00:03:15,369 --> 00:03:16,892
[chuckles]

75
00:03:16,979 --> 00:03:19,634
Patrick.

76
00:03:19,721 --> 00:03:22,506
This is nice.

77
00:03:22,593 --> 00:03:23,855
Been looking for you.
How you doing?

78
00:03:23,942 --> 00:03:24,943
Everything okay?

79
00:03:25,030 --> 00:03:26,031
Well, how you doing, Oscar?

80
00:03:26,118 --> 00:03:27,163
I'm good.
How you doing?

81
00:03:27,250 --> 00:03:29,121
Good. This is,
um, Lorelei.

82
00:03:29,209 --> 00:03:31,472
Lorelei? What are
you guys drinking?

83
00:03:31,559 --> 00:03:33,343
Uh, same again
for my friends here.

84
00:03:33,430 --> 00:03:36,738
Cognac for me.

85
00:03:36,825 --> 00:03:38,914
This is an amazing man
right here.

86
00:03:39,001 --> 00:03:40,002
Mm.

87
00:03:40,089 --> 00:03:41,003
This man can reach beyond

88
00:03:41,090 --> 00:03:42,265
the veil of death.

89
00:03:42,352 --> 00:03:44,485
- Did you know that?
- Uh, no.

90
00:03:44,572 --> 00:03:46,487
No, we-we just met, really.

91
00:03:46,574 --> 00:03:48,140
You ever lose someone?

92
00:03:48,228 --> 00:03:50,055
I lost my mother
when I was five.

93
00:03:50,142 --> 00:03:52,057
[clears throat]

94
00:03:52,144 --> 00:03:53,885
But this man..

95
00:03:53,972 --> 00:03:55,844
...he let me
talk to her.

96
00:03:55,931 --> 00:03:58,716
And I truly felt
her presence.

97
00:03:58,803 --> 00:03:59,935
She said
she loves me.

98
00:04:00,022 --> 00:04:02,503
She's always
watching over me.

99
00:04:02,590 --> 00:04:03,678
Wow.

100
00:04:03,765 --> 00:04:05,419
Well, it's both a gift..

101
00:04:05,506 --> 00:04:06,550
...and a curse.

102
00:04:06,637 --> 00:04:07,856
Yeah, well..

103
00:04:07,943 --> 00:04:09,466
[slurps]

104
00:04:09,553 --> 00:04:11,860
...I told my father
all about you.

105
00:04:11,947 --> 00:04:14,210
[Oscar]
'About, uh, what an awesome'

106
00:04:14,297 --> 00:04:15,733
'spiritual experience it was.'

107
00:04:15,820 --> 00:04:16,952
Mm-hmm.

108
00:04:17,039 --> 00:04:18,606
Best ten grand
I ever spent.

109
00:04:18,693 --> 00:04:20,172
My father,
he's a tight bastard.

110
00:04:20,260 --> 00:04:22,436
He says, "ten grand?

111
00:04:22,523 --> 00:04:23,872
"Screw that bitch.

112
00:04:23,959 --> 00:04:25,700
Go get your money back."

113
00:04:25,787 --> 00:04:27,832
Turns out
my mother's not dead.

114
00:04:27,919 --> 00:04:30,226
She ran off with
her aerobics instructor.

115
00:04:30,313 --> 00:04:32,620
She lives
in San Juan, Puerto Rico.

116
00:04:32,707 --> 00:04:35,536
'Owns a nail salon.'

117
00:04:35,623 --> 00:04:36,580
That explains why she was

118
00:04:36,667 --> 00:04:38,365
so easy to contact, I guess.

119
00:04:38,452 --> 00:04:40,236
[chuckles]

120
00:04:40,323 --> 00:04:42,151
[laughs]

121
00:04:42,238 --> 00:04:43,979
That's good
you can smile about this.

122
00:04:44,066 --> 00:04:46,068
- Here's the thing--
- 'I'm gonna be forgiving.'

123
00:04:46,155 --> 00:04:47,678
Give me my money back..

124
00:04:47,765 --> 00:04:49,419
...and, uh, Mervin
here is gonna tune you up

125
00:04:49,506 --> 00:04:51,943
a little, that's all.

126
00:04:52,030 --> 00:04:53,336
You, uh..

127
00:04:53,423 --> 00:04:55,077
...you mind if I, um..

128
00:04:55,164 --> 00:04:56,774
Give me
my money back.

129
00:04:56,861 --> 00:04:59,821
Yeah, um, can I?
Pass a light. Thanks.

130
00:04:59,908 --> 00:05:02,214
Um, I don't have it.

131
00:05:02,302 --> 00:05:04,478
I spent it all.

132
00:05:04,565 --> 00:05:06,349
Okay.

133
00:05:06,436 --> 00:05:07,437
Well, Mervin's
gonna break

134
00:05:07,524 --> 00:05:09,700
your arms
and the legs..

135
00:05:09,787 --> 00:05:12,181
...and then when
you're walking again..

136
00:05:12,268 --> 00:05:15,924
...you'll owe me 50 grand.

137
00:05:17,926 --> 00:05:20,407
- Ah!
- C'mon, let me.

138
00:05:20,494 --> 00:05:21,451
I got it,
I got it, I got it.

139
00:05:21,538 --> 00:05:24,062
Go get him.

140
00:05:24,149 --> 00:05:27,065
[dramatic music]

141
00:05:39,208 --> 00:05:41,602
[tires screeching]

142
00:05:42,690 --> 00:05:43,821
[car horn honks]

143
00:05:46,215 --> 00:05:49,131
[dramatic music]

144
00:05:52,352 --> 00:05:53,918
There he is.

145
00:05:54,005 --> 00:05:56,878
[music continues]

146
00:05:58,488 --> 00:06:00,882
[foot steps]

147
00:06:08,106 --> 00:06:09,281
Ah!

148
00:06:11,371 --> 00:06:12,502
[giggles]

149
00:06:14,896 --> 00:06:18,726
[Oscar]
'Where you going?'

150
00:06:18,813 --> 00:06:19,770
[grunting]

151
00:06:19,857 --> 00:06:21,642
[car siren waling]

152
00:06:21,729 --> 00:06:23,818
[groaning]

153
00:06:23,905 --> 00:06:25,515
[Oscar]
'Merv!'

154
00:06:25,602 --> 00:06:27,343
[man #2]
Police, hold it
right there!

155
00:06:27,430 --> 00:06:28,388
Alright, alright.

156
00:06:28,475 --> 00:06:30,390
Stay where you are.

157
00:06:30,477 --> 00:06:32,740
[man #3]
'Oscar stay. Don't move.'

158
00:06:32,827 --> 00:06:34,350
You all right?

159
00:06:34,437 --> 00:06:36,047
[grunting]

160
00:06:36,134 --> 00:06:38,528
[taser crackling]

161
00:06:41,488 --> 00:06:44,404
[instrumental music]

162
00:06:51,236 --> 00:06:53,543
[instrumental music]

163
00:06:54,936 --> 00:06:56,024
[Rigsby]
So Benjamin does this thing now

164
00:06:56,111 --> 00:06:57,068
where he kinda
scoots forward

165
00:06:57,155 --> 00:06:58,418
on his butt
like a penguin.

166
00:06:58,505 --> 00:07:00,202
- It's so cute, it's insane.
- Yeah.

167
00:07:00,289 --> 00:07:02,247
Oh, wait. I got a clip on my
phone. Let me find it for you.

168
00:07:02,334 --> 00:07:03,727
- Hey, T.
- Hey, Pat.

169
00:07:03,814 --> 00:07:05,599
[Pat]
How you doin'? Guys.

170
00:07:05,686 --> 00:07:07,035
- Hi.
- Hi.

171
00:07:07,122 --> 00:07:09,254
[Lisbon]
Oh, God.
What did that?

172
00:07:09,341 --> 00:07:11,866
Shotgun, from about
six inches away.

173
00:07:11,953 --> 00:07:13,563
John Doe all the way.

174
00:07:13,650 --> 00:07:15,478
No wallet, no tattoos

175
00:07:15,565 --> 00:07:17,349
no jewelry, no face.

176
00:07:17,437 --> 00:07:18,481
There's a lot of blood.

177
00:07:18,568 --> 00:07:19,787
He must've been killed
right here.

178
00:07:19,874 --> 00:07:21,353
Robbery?

179
00:07:21,441 --> 00:07:23,617
Well, there's
no foot traffic.

180
00:07:23,704 --> 00:07:26,315
Nothing but offices
around here. It's dead at night.

181
00:07:26,402 --> 00:07:28,186
Well, he must've arrived here
in some kind of vehicle.

182
00:07:28,273 --> 00:07:30,885
There's an interstate ramp
a block away from here.

183
00:07:30,972 --> 00:07:32,930
Our friend could've
come from Oregon.

184
00:07:33,017 --> 00:07:34,497
Give us 20 minutes with him,
and you can bag him.

185
00:07:34,584 --> 00:07:35,846
No hurry.

186
00:07:35,933 --> 00:07:38,196
Hey...sorry about
Jane, by the way.

187
00:07:38,283 --> 00:07:39,241
That's too bad.

188
00:07:39,328 --> 00:07:40,285
Too bad about what?

189
00:07:40,372 --> 00:07:42,679
That he got arrested.

190
00:07:42,766 --> 00:07:44,464
I heard it from
some guys in vice.

191
00:07:44,551 --> 00:07:46,988
He got busted
for assault, fraud..

192
00:07:47,075 --> 00:07:49,164
...narcotics
and resisting arrest..

193
00:07:49,251 --> 00:07:50,382
...in Vegas.

194
00:07:50,470 --> 00:07:51,558
That's terrible.

195
00:07:51,645 --> 00:07:52,907
We should do something.

196
00:07:52,994 --> 00:07:55,213
- Like what?
- I don't know.

197
00:07:55,300 --> 00:07:56,911
Try and talk
to him, I guess.

198
00:07:56,998 --> 00:07:58,347
See if he needs help.

199
00:07:58,434 --> 00:07:59,566
It's been six months
since he left.

200
00:07:59,653 --> 00:08:00,610
Maybe he's changed.

201
00:08:00,697 --> 00:08:02,177
- No.
- 'But--'

202
00:08:02,264 --> 00:08:04,048
I offered him
all the help in the world

203
00:08:04,135 --> 00:08:06,268
and he turned me
down many times.

204
00:08:06,355 --> 00:08:07,878
He has to want to change.

205
00:08:07,965 --> 00:08:09,358
He has to hit
bottom and know it.

206
00:08:09,445 --> 00:08:11,403
That's recovery
101, right?

207
00:08:11,491 --> 00:08:12,448
I guess.

208
00:08:12,535 --> 00:08:13,493
Well, maybe this is bottom.

209
00:08:13,580 --> 00:08:14,798
It's pretty low, boss.

210
00:08:14,885 --> 00:08:16,365
When he wants help,
he'll ask us.

211
00:08:16,452 --> 00:08:18,410
He knows where we are.

212
00:08:18,498 --> 00:08:20,369
- Hey, Pat. Good seeing you.
- You too.

213
00:08:20,456 --> 00:08:22,327
Get our John Doe
here on ice quick.

214
00:08:22,414 --> 00:08:23,851
I think he's gonna be
around for a while.

215
00:08:23,938 --> 00:08:26,070
[Pat]
'Alright, see you.'

216
00:08:26,157 --> 00:08:29,030
[instrumental music[

217
00:08:31,815 --> 00:08:33,251
[keys jangling]

218
00:08:39,301 --> 00:08:40,868
[door lock buzzing]

219
00:08:42,217 --> 00:08:44,088
- Sign that.
- Um.

220
00:08:44,175 --> 00:08:45,873
Ah.

221
00:08:45,960 --> 00:08:48,049
Uh, wh-why am I
being released?

222
00:08:48,136 --> 00:08:49,485
I didn't raise bail.

223
00:08:49,572 --> 00:08:51,356
Somebody raised it for you.

224
00:08:51,443 --> 00:08:53,402
Who was that?

225
00:08:53,489 --> 00:08:55,491
I don't have
that information.

226
00:08:55,578 --> 00:08:57,275
Teresa Lisbon is my guess.

227
00:08:57,362 --> 00:08:58,842
Huh? Lisbon?

228
00:08:58,929 --> 00:09:01,018
I don't have
that information.

229
00:09:01,105 --> 00:09:02,716
Okay. You don't have
that information.

230
00:09:02,803 --> 00:09:04,935
You can keep that.
Thank you.

231
00:09:05,022 --> 00:09:06,154
[sniffles]

232
00:09:07,851 --> 00:09:13,335
[sighs]

233
00:09:13,422 --> 00:09:14,554
Oy!

234
00:09:15,816 --> 00:09:18,688
[instrumental music]

235
00:09:29,090 --> 00:09:31,962
[music continues]

236
00:09:42,320 --> 00:09:45,236
[music continues]

237
00:09:48,849 --> 00:09:49,980
[sighs]

238
00:10:00,687 --> 00:10:03,603
[instrumental music]

239
00:10:09,565 --> 00:10:10,958
Boss.

240
00:10:11,045 --> 00:10:12,394
Good news, bad news.

241
00:10:12,481 --> 00:10:14,396
Bad news,
our John Doe's prints

242
00:10:14,483 --> 00:10:16,659
didn't get a match,
so we still have no ID.

243
00:10:16,746 --> 00:10:18,008
Of course.

244
00:10:18,095 --> 00:10:19,793
Good news, Sac PD
caught a homicide

245
00:10:19,880 --> 00:10:21,533
on Pacoima and third
last night.

246
00:10:21,621 --> 00:10:23,535
Suspect got away,
but they have an eyewitness

247
00:10:23,623 --> 00:10:25,494
and they recovered
the murder weapon.

248
00:10:25,581 --> 00:10:27,235
A sawed-off shotgun.

249
00:10:27,322 --> 00:10:29,106
Ejected cartridge was
the same make as ours

250
00:10:29,193 --> 00:10:30,586
and Pacoima and third
is only ten blocks

251
00:10:30,673 --> 00:10:31,805
from our murder scene.

252
00:10:31,892 --> 00:10:33,763
That's news,
good news would be

253
00:10:33,850 --> 00:10:35,504
better than that.

254
00:10:35,591 --> 00:10:37,201
- It's a lead.
- You're right.

255
00:10:37,288 --> 00:10:38,463
Sac PD, you said?

256
00:10:38,550 --> 00:10:40,161
Uh, who's the detective
on that?

257
00:10:40,248 --> 00:10:43,077
Not sure. Somebody on
Captain Rupert's night shift.

258
00:10:43,164 --> 00:10:44,339
You're right,
It's a good lead

259
00:10:44,426 --> 00:10:45,775
and I need to get
out of here.

260
00:10:45,862 --> 00:10:48,778
Let's go down in person
and see what they have.

261
00:10:51,999 --> 00:10:52,956
[knock on door]

262
00:10:53,043 --> 00:10:55,916
[instrumental music]

263
00:11:02,574 --> 00:11:03,706
Mm.

264
00:11:07,318 --> 00:11:08,624
Hey.

265
00:11:08,711 --> 00:11:10,452
Hey.

266
00:11:10,539 --> 00:11:12,149
Surprise.

267
00:11:12,236 --> 00:11:14,369
Yeah.

268
00:11:14,456 --> 00:11:16,501
Lorrie, right?

269
00:11:16,588 --> 00:11:18,068
Lorelei.

270
00:11:18,155 --> 00:11:19,896
Sorry.
This was a mistake.

271
00:11:19,983 --> 00:11:21,463
No, no, no. Lorelei.

272
00:11:21,550 --> 00:11:22,986
I'm very happy
to see you.

273
00:11:23,073 --> 00:11:24,901
Just, uh, been
a little slow today.

274
00:11:24,988 --> 00:11:26,860
It's...it's been
a rough week.

275
00:11:26,947 --> 00:11:29,993
Yeah, I can imagine.

276
00:11:30,080 --> 00:11:32,866
I...brought you
some chicken soup.

277
00:11:32,953 --> 00:11:34,519
For me?

278
00:11:34,606 --> 00:11:36,130
Yeah.

279
00:11:36,217 --> 00:11:38,654
Come in.

280
00:11:40,134 --> 00:11:42,745
Excuse the mess.

281
00:11:42,832 --> 00:11:44,921
How did you know
my address?

282
00:11:45,008 --> 00:11:48,446
The bail bondsman
gave it to me.

283
00:11:48,533 --> 00:11:50,187
How did you know
who the bail bondsman was?

284
00:11:50,274 --> 00:11:51,362
[chuckles]

285
00:11:51,449 --> 00:11:52,929
What are you,
Columbo here

286
00:11:53,016 --> 00:11:54,278
with the third degree?

287
00:11:54,365 --> 00:11:58,326
I'm sorry.
Just a little curious.

288
00:11:58,413 --> 00:12:02,199
I knew who he was,
because...I was the one

289
00:12:02,286 --> 00:12:04,941
that put up the money
for your bail.

290
00:12:05,028 --> 00:12:07,465
That's a lot of money.

291
00:12:07,552 --> 00:12:09,511
I'll-I'll pay you back
as soon as I can.

292
00:12:09,598 --> 00:12:12,383
Figured you were
good for it.

293
00:12:12,470 --> 00:12:13,602
Why'd you
do that for me?

294
00:12:13,689 --> 00:12:15,343
[inhales deeply]

295
00:12:15,430 --> 00:12:18,433
You seemed like
a good man who lost his way.

296
00:12:18,520 --> 00:12:21,392
I could help,
so I did.

297
00:12:21,479 --> 00:12:22,829
And at this point

298
00:12:22,916 --> 00:12:26,658
a straight up
"thank you" would be okay.

299
00:12:26,746 --> 00:12:29,836
Thank you.

300
00:12:29,923 --> 00:12:34,231
There's, uh...a lot
of good men out there..

301
00:12:34,318 --> 00:12:37,060
...who have lost their way.

302
00:12:37,147 --> 00:12:38,670
Wow. You're gonna
make me say it out loud?

303
00:12:38,758 --> 00:12:40,063
[chuckles]

304
00:12:40,150 --> 00:12:43,806
I felt like
we got along pretty good.

305
00:12:43,893 --> 00:12:45,503
I felt like
there was some kind of..

306
00:12:45,590 --> 00:12:46,940
[gasps]

307
00:12:47,027 --> 00:12:48,550
...weird connection
there between us.

308
00:12:48,637 --> 00:12:52,075
I trusted my feelings.

309
00:12:53,903 --> 00:12:56,906
Damn it. Was I wrong?

310
00:12:57,907 --> 00:13:00,344
No.

311
00:13:00,431 --> 00:13:02,259
You weren't wrong.

312
00:13:02,346 --> 00:13:03,826
Okay then.

313
00:13:03,913 --> 00:13:05,610
I have to
warn you, Lorelei.

314
00:13:05,697 --> 00:13:07,787
Um, I'm not
the great catch

315
00:13:07,874 --> 00:13:11,355
you might think
I am from..

316
00:13:11,442 --> 00:13:14,141
...first impressions.

317
00:13:15,707 --> 00:13:16,752
That's okay.

318
00:13:16,839 --> 00:13:19,711
Neither am I.

319
00:13:22,845 --> 00:13:26,022
Bean, tell these people
what you saw.

320
00:13:26,109 --> 00:13:27,676
I'm collecting
cans on third.

321
00:13:27,763 --> 00:13:30,200
Right next to the park
where they sell their drugs.

322
00:13:30,287 --> 00:13:32,028
There's a gunshot. Boom!

323
00:13:32,115 --> 00:13:33,943
Then a tall,
young, Latin gentleman

324
00:13:34,030 --> 00:13:35,162
come running
out of the park

325
00:13:35,249 --> 00:13:37,425
holding
a sawed-off shotgun.

326
00:13:37,512 --> 00:13:39,122
He trips and falls over.

327
00:13:39,209 --> 00:13:40,907
[chuckles]
Drops the gun.

328
00:13:40,994 --> 00:13:43,431
Then he gets up
and runs away..

329
00:13:43,518 --> 00:13:45,912
...leaves the gun,
and that's what I saw.

330
00:13:45,999 --> 00:13:47,827
The tall, young,
Latin gentleman..

331
00:13:47,914 --> 00:13:49,393
...did you get
a good look at him?

332
00:13:49,480 --> 00:13:50,917
Come right by me.

333
00:13:51,004 --> 00:13:52,919
Got a scar
on his face right here.

334
00:13:53,006 --> 00:13:54,616
- Little chin beard.
- Mm-hmm.

335
00:13:54,703 --> 00:13:57,140
Big gold earring
like a pirate.

336
00:13:57,227 --> 00:13:59,621
Black t-shirt, jeans..

337
00:13:59,708 --> 00:14:01,144
...white shoes.

338
00:14:01,231 --> 00:14:04,017
Anything on the t-shirt?
Logo? Numbers?

339
00:14:04,104 --> 00:14:05,801
- Don't think so.
- Thanks, Bean.

340
00:14:05,888 --> 00:14:09,718
Wait. Close your eyes
and picture him.

341
00:14:11,851 --> 00:14:14,592
Now imagine
him coming toward you.

342
00:14:14,679 --> 00:14:16,290
Oh!

343
00:14:16,377 --> 00:14:19,380
There's a little dog
right here on his shirt.

344
00:14:19,467 --> 00:14:20,990
Not a cute dog.

345
00:14:21,077 --> 00:14:22,035
Like, you know

346
00:14:22,122 --> 00:14:23,906
a snarling dog.

347
00:14:23,993 --> 00:14:25,734
Like a bulldog or a wolf?

348
00:14:25,821 --> 00:14:27,214
Wolf!

349
00:14:27,301 --> 00:14:28,911
Grape Street lobos
wear black shirts

350
00:14:28,998 --> 00:14:30,173
with a wolf on 'em.

351
00:14:30,260 --> 00:14:32,262
- Thank you, Miss Bean.
- Mm-hmm.

352
00:14:32,349 --> 00:14:34,482
Yeah, so it's kind
of thin but my guys

353
00:14:34,569 --> 00:14:36,701
will check out the lobos
and we'll let you know.

354
00:14:36,788 --> 00:14:38,442
[Van Pelt]
Well, we can check 'em out
for you, if you'd like.

355
00:14:38,529 --> 00:14:40,009
CBI gang unit has
a really good database.

356
00:14:40,096 --> 00:14:41,228
That's okay, girls.

357
00:14:41,315 --> 00:14:42,272
Thanks, but we
don't even know

358
00:14:42,359 --> 00:14:43,317
if it's the same
gun as yours.

359
00:14:43,404 --> 00:14:44,666
It probably isn't.

360
00:14:44,753 --> 00:14:45,972
Yeah, okay, Rupe.
It was good seeing you.

361
00:14:46,059 --> 00:14:47,190
Yeah.

362
00:14:48,626 --> 00:14:49,714
Talk to the gang unit.

363
00:14:49,801 --> 00:14:51,325
See what they know
about the lobos.

364
00:14:51,412 --> 00:14:52,674
Okay.

365
00:14:52,761 --> 00:14:53,936
I'm gonna take
some personal time.

366
00:14:54,023 --> 00:14:55,895
You take the car.
I'm gonna walk.

367
00:14:55,982 --> 00:14:57,026
Walk?

368
00:14:57,113 --> 00:14:59,246
I mean...okay.

369
00:14:59,333 --> 00:15:01,248
See you.

370
00:15:02,423 --> 00:15:05,295
[instrumental music]

371
00:15:11,040 --> 00:15:14,739
[man on TV]
'The zebra's kick
savesits life.'

372
00:15:17,090 --> 00:15:20,484
Oh. She got away.

373
00:15:22,573 --> 00:15:24,924
'But a neck bite
finally subdues her prey.'

374
00:15:25,011 --> 00:15:26,142
[gasps]

375
00:15:27,883 --> 00:15:30,320
- Mm.
- You okay?

376
00:15:30,407 --> 00:15:33,933
'Brings several months
supply of regular meals.'

377
00:15:38,198 --> 00:15:40,591
[instrumental music]

378
00:15:46,380 --> 00:15:49,252
[music continues]

379
00:15:59,393 --> 00:16:02,265
[music continues]

380
00:16:05,616 --> 00:16:08,532
[sizzling]

381
00:16:12,667 --> 00:16:15,539
[instrumental music]

382
00:16:23,199 --> 00:16:25,636
Good morning.

383
00:16:25,723 --> 00:16:27,987
[chuckles]

384
00:16:28,074 --> 00:16:31,991
Good morning,
sleepy lover.

385
00:16:35,429 --> 00:16:36,430
Mm.

386
00:16:36,517 --> 00:16:39,346
You must have
slept 12 hours.

387
00:16:39,433 --> 00:16:40,695
Yeah, I think I was tired.

388
00:16:40,782 --> 00:16:42,479
Mm-hmm.

389
00:16:42,566 --> 00:16:44,351
I gotta go to work.

390
00:16:44,438 --> 00:16:45,874
I made some eggs.

391
00:16:45,961 --> 00:16:50,574
How did you know
I love eggs?

392
00:16:50,661 --> 00:16:53,142
[sniffles]

393
00:16:53,229 --> 00:16:57,538
This is delicious.
Thank you.

394
00:16:57,625 --> 00:16:58,974
We had fun, huh?

395
00:16:59,061 --> 00:17:00,193
Yeah.

396
00:17:03,065 --> 00:17:05,676
Perhaps we can see
each other again.

397
00:17:05,763 --> 00:17:07,678
That's not up to me.

398
00:17:07,765 --> 00:17:09,463
Oh, you have no say in it?

399
00:17:09,550 --> 00:17:11,465
None at all.

400
00:17:11,552 --> 00:17:13,728
He's very restful.

401
00:17:13,815 --> 00:17:15,730
I don't follow you.

402
00:17:15,817 --> 00:17:20,387
I do what Red John
tells me to do.

403
00:17:20,474 --> 00:17:21,649
What?

404
00:17:23,520 --> 00:17:24,869
Your freedom..

405
00:17:24,956 --> 00:17:25,914
...our night together.

406
00:17:26,001 --> 00:17:29,135
That was a gift from him.

407
00:17:30,571 --> 00:17:34,053
You can hurt me,
if you'd like.

408
00:17:34,140 --> 00:17:36,533
No, I don't want
to hurt you.

409
00:17:36,620 --> 00:17:39,971
I've given up.
He knows that.

410
00:17:40,059 --> 00:17:41,277
What does
he want from me?

411
00:17:41,364 --> 00:17:44,280
He doesn't want
anything from you.

412
00:17:44,367 --> 00:17:46,152
After all these years..

413
00:17:46,239 --> 00:17:47,849
...he's come
to see you as an..

414
00:17:47,936 --> 00:17:50,982
...old comrade
rather than an enemy.

415
00:17:51,070 --> 00:17:53,333
He hopes you'll come
to feel the same way.

416
00:17:53,420 --> 00:17:55,422
A comrade.

417
00:17:56,771 --> 00:17:59,469
Patrick..

418
00:17:59,556 --> 00:18:01,950
...look at yourself.

419
00:18:02,037 --> 00:18:04,431
You need a new life.

420
00:18:04,518 --> 00:18:07,129
He can give
that to you.

421
00:18:07,216 --> 00:18:08,522
You have to leave.

422
00:18:08,609 --> 00:18:10,654
He's offering
the hand of friendship.

423
00:18:10,741 --> 00:18:13,048
If you refuse him,
he'll be upset.

424
00:18:13,135 --> 00:18:16,965
- Anyone would be.
- Get out.

425
00:18:22,013 --> 00:18:24,929
You know
where to find me.

426
00:18:27,367 --> 00:18:30,239
[instrumental music]

427
00:18:39,205 --> 00:18:41,337
[instrumental music]

428
00:18:43,600 --> 00:18:45,602
Hey, Grace,
you seen Lisbon?

429
00:18:45,689 --> 00:18:47,691
She had to take
some personal time.

430
00:18:47,778 --> 00:18:48,910
Where'd she go?

431
00:18:48,997 --> 00:18:50,216
Didn't say.

432
00:18:50,303 --> 00:18:51,608
We have a lead.

433
00:18:51,695 --> 00:18:53,393
I just got this
from the gang unit.

434
00:18:53,480 --> 00:18:56,135
Kevin Cintron,
aka Purple.

435
00:18:56,222 --> 00:18:58,833
Affiliated with
the Grape Street Lobos.

436
00:18:58,920 --> 00:19:00,661
Matches the witness
description exactly.

437
00:19:00,748 --> 00:19:02,184
Did you show
the witness the photo?

438
00:19:02,271 --> 00:19:03,446
I do that,
and we have to go through

439
00:19:03,533 --> 00:19:04,969
Sac PD Homicide
and they'll wanna

440
00:19:05,056 --> 00:19:06,362
take the bust
and we need the bust.

441
00:19:06,449 --> 00:19:07,755
Must be a thousand bad guys

442
00:19:07,842 --> 00:19:09,452
with gold earrings,
beards and scars.

443
00:19:09,539 --> 00:19:11,324
I got an address
from his PO.

444
00:19:11,411 --> 00:19:13,543
After killing two people that's
probably not where he's at.

445
00:19:13,630 --> 00:19:16,416
It's a good place to start,
though, and I'm going.

446
00:19:16,503 --> 00:19:19,419
You want me to get you
some doughnuts while I'm out?

447
00:19:20,942 --> 00:19:22,117
[bell chiming]

448
00:19:23,945 --> 00:19:26,817
[instrumental music]

449
00:19:36,871 --> 00:19:39,743
[music continues]

450
00:19:55,106 --> 00:19:56,586
[Patrick]
'This is God.'

451
00:19:56,673 --> 00:19:57,979
'What is it now?'

452
00:19:58,066 --> 00:19:59,633
[laughing]

453
00:19:59,720 --> 00:20:00,938
You scared
the life out of me.

454
00:20:01,025 --> 00:20:02,462
[exhales sharply]

455
00:20:02,549 --> 00:20:04,115
I crawled
all the way on my

456
00:20:04,203 --> 00:20:06,770
hands and knees
from that door.

457
00:20:06,857 --> 00:20:09,077
- But it was worth it.
- What are you doing here?

458
00:20:09,164 --> 00:20:10,948
It's good to see you.
How have you been?

459
00:20:11,035 --> 00:20:12,646
Worried sick
is how I've been

460
00:20:12,733 --> 00:20:14,909
and then you pop in here
like some sort of a lunatic

461
00:20:14,996 --> 00:20:16,824
playing games,
asking me how I've been.

462
00:20:16,911 --> 00:20:17,999
- Just--
- Shame on you.

463
00:20:18,086 --> 00:20:19,566
Stay calm, okay?

464
00:20:19,653 --> 00:20:21,263
It's important that
no one sees us together.

465
00:20:21,350 --> 00:20:22,612
[sighs]

466
00:20:22,699 --> 00:20:25,398
Why not?

467
00:20:25,485 --> 00:20:27,791
I'm faking my breakdown.

468
00:20:27,878 --> 00:20:29,924
It's a ruse
to trap Red John.

469
00:20:30,011 --> 00:20:32,753
You son of a bitch.

470
00:20:32,840 --> 00:20:34,972
You...son of a bitch.

471
00:20:35,059 --> 00:20:36,713
Okay, we are in a church.

472
00:20:36,800 --> 00:20:39,107
Uh, wait, so how does
faking a breakdown

473
00:20:39,194 --> 00:20:41,022
if that's what
you're reallydoing

474
00:20:41,109 --> 00:20:42,415
because it looks
pretty real to me

475
00:20:42,502 --> 00:20:44,678
how does that
trap Red John?

476
00:20:44,765 --> 00:20:46,636
What does
Red John want from me?

477
00:20:46,723 --> 00:20:49,813
What did he send
that little girl to ask me?

478
00:20:49,900 --> 00:20:52,163
- Do you give up?
- Exactly, and I do give up.

479
00:20:52,251 --> 00:20:54,383
I quit. I burn
the Red John files.

480
00:20:54,470 --> 00:20:56,167
I freak out
at the boss.

481
00:20:56,255 --> 00:20:57,865
I admit defeat,
and I sink

482
00:20:57,952 --> 00:21:00,737
into a terrible
depression.

483
00:21:00,824 --> 00:21:02,086
Brilliant.
You did that part great.

484
00:21:02,173 --> 00:21:03,262
Now what?

485
00:21:03,349 --> 00:21:05,438
And why doesn't
he just kill me?

486
00:21:05,525 --> 00:21:06,874
Because it's too easy.

487
00:21:06,961 --> 00:21:08,136
He wants to turn me.

488
00:21:08,223 --> 00:21:10,617
He wants to make
me his disciple.

489
00:21:10,704 --> 00:21:14,142
So I admit defeat,
and then he reaches out

490
00:21:14,229 --> 00:21:16,231
to start a conversation.

491
00:21:16,318 --> 00:21:17,841
That's all
supposition.

492
00:21:17,928 --> 00:21:19,582
- He's not gonna--
- He already has reached out.

493
00:21:19,669 --> 00:21:22,803
He sent me
a message.

494
00:21:22,890 --> 00:21:25,109
I need to
start a new life

495
00:21:25,196 --> 00:21:28,417
and he can help me.

496
00:21:28,504 --> 00:21:29,592
Help you?

497
00:21:29,679 --> 00:21:32,160
He wants to help you?

498
00:21:32,247 --> 00:21:33,596
- Yeah.
- What are you gonna do?

499
00:21:33,683 --> 00:21:36,730
Well, I'm gonna
take him up on the offer.

500
00:21:36,817 --> 00:21:38,732
I'm in a lot
of real trouble.

501
00:21:38,819 --> 00:21:40,037
I do need
a new life.

502
00:21:40,124 --> 00:21:41,778
Yes, you do.

503
00:21:41,865 --> 00:21:45,086
That's what makes
the gag work.

504
00:21:45,173 --> 00:21:46,435
- Then what?
- Well, I don't know.

505
00:21:46,522 --> 00:21:47,480
I let him lead.

506
00:21:47,567 --> 00:21:49,133
That's the beauty of it.

507
00:21:49,220 --> 00:21:50,396
He thinks I'm the fish

508
00:21:50,483 --> 00:21:51,440
and he's the fisherman.

509
00:21:51,527 --> 00:21:54,443
Unless he sees the truth.

510
00:21:54,530 --> 00:21:56,663
I am giving him
his heart's desire.

511
00:21:56,750 --> 00:21:59,753
He will see
what he wants to see.

512
00:21:59,840 --> 00:22:01,232
Or not.

513
00:22:01,320 --> 00:22:02,973
Fooled you.
I can fool him.

514
00:22:03,060 --> 00:22:05,541
Yeah, you fooled me
all right. Well done.

515
00:22:05,628 --> 00:22:06,629
Yeah.

516
00:22:06,716 --> 00:22:08,501
Well..

517
00:22:08,588 --> 00:22:11,547
...I'm sorry.

518
00:22:11,634 --> 00:22:12,983
I tried calling.

519
00:22:13,070 --> 00:22:14,507
I...tried calling you

520
00:22:14,594 --> 00:22:15,986
hundreds...of times.

521
00:22:16,073 --> 00:22:17,510
Begging you
to talk to me.

522
00:22:17,597 --> 00:22:19,512
Begging you
to get help.

523
00:22:19,599 --> 00:22:21,078
Not a reply.

524
00:22:21,165 --> 00:22:22,123
Not a word.

525
00:22:22,210 --> 00:22:24,734
Not a text.

526
00:22:25,605 --> 00:22:26,736
Sorry.

527
00:22:26,823 --> 00:22:28,390
You know what?

528
00:22:28,477 --> 00:22:29,826
I have not
been sleeping.

529
00:22:29,913 --> 00:22:31,219
I've been...forget it.

530
00:22:31,306 --> 00:22:32,481
Never mind.

531
00:22:32,568 --> 00:22:35,441
You know,
y-you're a jerk.

532
00:22:37,181 --> 00:22:38,966
And your plan?
It's stupid.

533
00:22:39,053 --> 00:22:42,099
It's not even a plan.

534
00:22:43,100 --> 00:22:44,928
But you will help me?

535
00:22:45,015 --> 00:22:47,366
What am I
supposed to say, no?

536
00:22:47,453 --> 00:22:49,933
God, you're despicable.

537
00:22:50,020 --> 00:22:52,109
Take this.
It's clean.

538
00:22:52,196 --> 00:22:53,633
I'll call you on it
when the time comes.

539
00:22:53,720 --> 00:22:55,504
In the meantime,
do not contact me.

540
00:22:55,591 --> 00:22:58,377
Do not let anyone
from CBI contact me.

541
00:22:58,464 --> 00:23:00,988
And don't tell
anyone the truth.

542
00:23:01,075 --> 00:23:03,120
Not a soul.

543
00:23:03,207 --> 00:23:04,948
I cannot believe
you didn't tell me

544
00:23:05,035 --> 00:23:06,472
you were doing this,
that you couldn't trust me

545
00:23:06,559 --> 00:23:07,690
with a secret like that.

546
00:23:07,777 --> 00:23:09,518
We're supposed
to be partners.

547
00:23:09,605 --> 00:23:11,128
God knows,
I am happy you're back.

548
00:23:11,215 --> 00:23:12,434
It is a huge relief.

549
00:23:12,521 --> 00:23:14,262
But what you did..

550
00:23:14,349 --> 00:23:17,787
...frankly, was a betrayal.

551
00:23:19,049 --> 00:23:21,008
God, I hate you, Jane.

552
00:23:21,095 --> 00:23:24,098
I hate you!

553
00:23:27,841 --> 00:23:30,234
We have your prints
on the shotgun, Kevin.

554
00:23:30,321 --> 00:23:31,584
We have an eyewitness
who saw you shoot

555
00:23:31,671 --> 00:23:34,282
Dashawn Willits
with that shotgun.

556
00:23:34,369 --> 00:23:35,326
I'm showing them
the gun because

557
00:23:35,414 --> 00:23:36,763
I'm trying to
sell it to 'em.

558
00:23:36,850 --> 00:23:37,807
Fool tried to take
the gun from me.

559
00:23:37,894 --> 00:23:39,069
I had no other choice.

560
00:23:39,156 --> 00:23:40,419
But the first
shooting, though.

561
00:23:40,506 --> 00:23:41,811
The white John Doe
on Lincoln Avenue.

562
00:23:41,898 --> 00:23:43,596
Did that guy try to
steal your gun, too?

563
00:23:43,683 --> 00:23:45,075
I didn't touch
that man, all right?

564
00:23:45,162 --> 00:23:48,209
He killed himself.

565
00:23:48,296 --> 00:23:50,603
I swear to god.
Me and my boy, Manfreddo

566
00:23:50,690 --> 00:23:52,039
we cruisin' down
the alleyway, we lookin' for

567
00:23:52,126 --> 00:23:54,171
open windows,
to be honest with you.

568
00:23:54,258 --> 00:23:56,478
I see this guy sittin'
up against the dumpster.

569
00:23:56,565 --> 00:23:59,263
Got a bicycle next to him
and a sawed-off shotgun.

570
00:23:59,350 --> 00:24:01,352
Just as we start
to get close...

571
00:24:01,440 --> 00:24:02,789
Damn if he don't
blow off his head.

572
00:24:02,876 --> 00:24:05,269
Hara-kiri.
No messing around.

573
00:24:05,356 --> 00:24:06,662
How do we know
you're telling the truth?

574
00:24:06,749 --> 00:24:10,361
You don't.
You just know what is.

575
00:24:10,449 --> 00:24:12,276
Come on, man,
you guys ask Manfreddo.

576
00:24:12,363 --> 00:24:15,541
He gonna tell
you the same thing.

577
00:24:15,628 --> 00:24:17,978
Yeah. Man just shot himself.

578
00:24:18,065 --> 00:24:20,023
Boom! Freaked me out.

579
00:24:20,110 --> 00:24:21,808
I wanted the gun,
but Kevin took it.

580
00:24:21,895 --> 00:24:24,114
I got the bike.
Sweet fixie.

581
00:24:24,201 --> 00:24:25,115
Where's the bike,
Manfreddo?

582
00:24:25,202 --> 00:24:27,596
Got stolen.

583
00:24:28,771 --> 00:24:30,991
I know.
Ironic, right?

584
00:24:31,078 --> 00:24:32,601
Did you take
anything else from him?

585
00:24:32,688 --> 00:24:35,952
We looked.
He had nothing on him.

586
00:24:36,039 --> 00:24:38,128
I think he's telling
the truth, Cintron admitted

587
00:24:38,215 --> 00:24:39,913
to the second
killing no problem.

588
00:24:40,000 --> 00:24:41,305
Why would he
lie about this one?

589
00:24:41,392 --> 00:24:43,264
Looks like
we'll never know who he was.

590
00:24:43,351 --> 00:24:45,222
- Poor soul.
- Mm.

591
00:24:45,309 --> 00:24:46,267
Lisbon, a word?

592
00:24:46,354 --> 00:24:48,574
Yeah.

593
00:24:48,661 --> 00:24:51,141
Uh, is that the John Doe
case you're working on?

594
00:24:51,228 --> 00:24:53,361
Yes, sir. It looks
to be a suicide.

595
00:24:53,448 --> 00:24:55,581
Oh, good. Excellent.
Get that off the books, eh?

596
00:24:55,668 --> 00:24:58,540
Um...I wanted
to talk to you about Jane.

597
00:24:58,627 --> 00:25:00,107
It's been six months
since he's gone.

598
00:25:00,194 --> 00:25:02,370
I think it's time
for a little outreach.

599
00:25:02,457 --> 00:25:03,980
Well, it's the humane
thing to do.

600
00:25:04,067 --> 00:25:05,939
He was a big part
of the CBI family, after all.

601
00:25:06,026 --> 00:25:06,983
I suppose, but--

602
00:25:07,070 --> 00:25:08,158
I jus-I...I just wanna

603
00:25:08,245 --> 00:25:09,682
give him a call, see if..

604
00:25:09,769 --> 00:25:11,510
...you know, I can't
persuade him into rehab

605
00:25:11,597 --> 00:25:12,946
or a psychiatry
program or some such.

606
00:25:13,033 --> 00:25:14,077
You know, it could
make a big difference

607
00:25:14,164 --> 00:25:15,470
in his sentencing.

608
00:25:15,557 --> 00:25:17,428
He could get
community service.

609
00:25:17,516 --> 00:25:19,561
He could come back
and work for us eventually.

610
00:25:19,648 --> 00:25:22,651
God knows...we need him.

611
00:25:22,738 --> 00:25:25,175
Closure rates being what
they are right now...low.

612
00:25:25,262 --> 00:25:27,656
Yes, sir, and we will
do our bestto fix that

613
00:25:27,743 --> 00:25:30,006
but I don't think
we can help Jane.

614
00:25:30,093 --> 00:25:32,226
Besides, yeah,
he's made his bed.

615
00:25:32,313 --> 00:25:34,968
I don't...think
I could work with him again.

616
00:25:35,055 --> 00:25:37,666
I need someone
I can rely on.

617
00:25:37,753 --> 00:25:39,059
I'm surprised.

618
00:25:39,146 --> 00:25:40,974
I thought you
would wanna help him.

619
00:25:41,061 --> 00:25:43,411
Well, I do.

620
00:25:43,498 --> 00:25:44,673
It's not how it looks.

621
00:25:44,760 --> 00:25:46,893
I just have a feeling
Jane's better off

622
00:25:46,980 --> 00:25:48,764
left alone right now.

623
00:25:48,851 --> 00:25:51,767
Okay.
It was just a thought.

624
00:25:51,854 --> 00:25:54,727
[instrumental music]

625
00:25:58,818 --> 00:26:00,428
I've been, um,
I've been thinking about

626
00:26:00,515 --> 00:26:02,604
what you said
about your friend.

627
00:26:02,691 --> 00:26:04,301
Yes.

628
00:26:04,388 --> 00:26:05,520
You said that
he could help me

629
00:26:05,607 --> 00:26:07,740
start a new life.

630
00:26:07,827 --> 00:26:11,352
- Right?
- Mm-hmm.

631
00:26:11,439 --> 00:26:14,268
What does
that mean exactly?

632
00:26:14,355 --> 00:26:17,532
A new identity...money.

633
00:26:17,619 --> 00:26:19,708
A place to live.
A job, if you want one.

634
00:26:19,795 --> 00:26:22,581
And I-I do what
in exchange?

635
00:26:22,668 --> 00:26:25,105
Accept his friendship.

636
00:26:25,192 --> 00:26:27,673
- It's that easy?
- Sure.

637
00:26:27,760 --> 00:26:30,153
He-he'll wanna
speak to you first.

638
00:26:30,240 --> 00:26:31,372
Make sure
you're on the level.

639
00:26:31,459 --> 00:26:33,374
If that's all right.

640
00:26:33,461 --> 00:26:34,854
Yeah.

641
00:26:34,941 --> 00:26:37,726
And you'll need
to bring him a gift..

642
00:26:37,813 --> 00:26:40,816
...to show your
respect for him.

643
00:26:40,903 --> 00:26:42,339
What kind of gift?

644
00:26:42,426 --> 00:26:44,254
Well..

645
00:26:44,341 --> 00:26:45,995
...Teresa Lisbon's
dead body

646
00:26:46,082 --> 00:26:47,475
would be
the perfect thing.

647
00:26:47,562 --> 00:26:50,478
[laughing]

648
00:26:51,348 --> 00:26:53,742
That's absurd.

649
00:26:55,091 --> 00:26:57,964
[instrumental music]

650
00:27:00,183 --> 00:27:02,708
What did
you tell me?

651
00:27:02,795 --> 00:27:05,798
There is no
right or wrong.

652
00:27:05,885 --> 00:27:08,017
There's just stuff
that happens.

653
00:27:08,104 --> 00:27:11,673
No, no, there-there
has to be something else.

654
00:27:11,760 --> 00:27:12,761
[sighs]

655
00:27:12,848 --> 00:27:14,023
I can't think
of anything else

656
00:27:14,110 --> 00:27:15,111
that would
please him.

657
00:27:15,198 --> 00:27:18,288
Well, I can't do that.

658
00:27:18,375 --> 00:27:22,075
I understand
you're not there yet.

659
00:27:22,162 --> 00:27:25,600
But look at it
from his point of view.

660
00:27:25,687 --> 00:27:28,255
How else will he know
you've trulyhad

661
00:27:28,342 --> 00:27:31,606
a change of heart?

662
00:27:31,693 --> 00:27:34,609
[dramatic music]

663
00:27:38,482 --> 00:27:41,398
[elevator bell dings]

664
00:27:41,485 --> 00:27:43,487
- Jane.
- Not now.

665
00:27:43,574 --> 00:27:47,056
Alright, I'm glad
to see that..

666
00:27:47,143 --> 00:27:50,016
[music continues]

667
00:27:56,762 --> 00:28:00,940
[Van Pelt]
'Jane.'

668
00:28:01,027 --> 00:28:02,593
Jane.

669
00:28:02,681 --> 00:28:03,899
Well.

670
00:28:03,986 --> 00:28:07,076
It's good
to see you all.

671
00:28:07,163 --> 00:28:08,121
How are you?

672
00:28:08,208 --> 00:28:10,384
Uh, we're good.
How are you?

673
00:28:10,471 --> 00:28:11,951
Never better.

674
00:28:12,038 --> 00:28:13,169
Never better.

675
00:28:13,256 --> 00:28:15,128
Jane?

676
00:28:15,215 --> 00:28:17,826
There you are.

677
00:28:19,393 --> 00:28:22,309
[ominous music]

678
00:28:30,578 --> 00:28:31,535
Good luck, Teresa.

679
00:28:31,622 --> 00:28:33,015
[cocks gun]

680
00:28:33,102 --> 00:28:34,495
Love you.

681
00:28:34,582 --> 00:28:35,714
[gunfire]

682
00:28:40,327 --> 00:28:42,677
[dramatic music]

683
00:28:45,680 --> 00:28:48,596
[crying]

684
00:28:57,257 --> 00:28:59,650
What happened?

685
00:29:01,565 --> 00:29:02,697
[crying]

686
00:29:02,784 --> 00:29:05,613
- What happened?
- Patrick Jane.

687
00:29:05,700 --> 00:29:08,442
[Cho]
'He took Lisbon.'

688
00:29:08,529 --> 00:29:11,358
Is he...oh,
oh, my God!

689
00:29:11,445 --> 00:29:13,577
Uff, his face, who..

690
00:29:13,664 --> 00:29:16,580
...who-who is th-who is that?

691
00:29:16,667 --> 00:29:19,583
It's Rigsby.

692
00:29:19,670 --> 00:29:20,671
[Cho]
'It's Wayne Rigsby.'

693
00:29:20,759 --> 00:29:22,978
[crying]

694
00:29:23,065 --> 00:29:25,894
Check, move forward, contain.

695
00:29:27,635 --> 00:29:30,029
Turn it up.

696
00:29:32,771 --> 00:29:35,251
[woman on TV]
'In a macabre twist,
after killing Agent Rigsby.'

697
00:29:35,338 --> 00:29:37,558
34-year-old
father of a baby boy

698
00:29:37,645 --> 00:29:39,255
the suspect, Patrick Jane

699
00:29:39,342 --> 00:29:40,822
took Agent Teresa Lisbon

700
00:29:40,909 --> 00:29:42,476
'presumed dead,
away with him'

701
00:29:42,563 --> 00:29:43,738
when he escaped.

702
00:29:43,825 --> 00:29:45,435
Authorities
will not speculate

703
00:29:45,522 --> 00:29:49,135
as to why he wants
her dead body.

704
00:29:53,879 --> 00:29:55,402
Oh. I'm hungry.

705
00:29:55,489 --> 00:29:56,795
I'm going
to the store for nachos.

706
00:29:56,882 --> 00:29:57,839
You guys want anything?

707
00:29:57,926 --> 00:29:59,362
They got pizza, hot dogs.

708
00:29:59,449 --> 00:30:00,537
I'm good.

709
00:30:00,624 --> 00:30:02,757
Me, too. Uh, Rigsby.

710
00:30:02,844 --> 00:30:04,193
[Rigsby]
'Yeah, I know, I know.'

711
00:30:04,280 --> 00:30:06,413
Don't call Sarah. I know.

712
00:30:06,500 --> 00:30:07,588
It's killing me, though.

713
00:30:07,675 --> 00:30:08,807
She must be
freaking out.

714
00:30:08,894 --> 00:30:09,895
Well, look
at the bright side.

715
00:30:09,982 --> 00:30:11,244
Think of how happy
she's gonna be

716
00:30:11,331 --> 00:30:12,898
when you come
back to life.

717
00:30:12,985 --> 00:30:14,116
Huh.

718
00:30:20,035 --> 00:30:22,342
So where'd you
find this place?

719
00:30:22,429 --> 00:30:23,517
The owner
owes me poker money

720
00:30:23,604 --> 00:30:24,997
he'll never pay back.

721
00:30:25,084 --> 00:30:26,215
Oh.

722
00:30:27,956 --> 00:30:28,957
So that thing you said

723
00:30:29,044 --> 00:30:31,177
before you shot me.

724
00:30:31,264 --> 00:30:33,657
Uh, what did you mean?

725
00:30:36,573 --> 00:30:38,532
What did I say?

726
00:30:38,619 --> 00:30:41,709
- I was kinda hyped up.
- Oh, boy. Me, too.

727
00:30:41,796 --> 00:30:43,885
I thought at any moment
we were gonna get found out.

728
00:30:43,972 --> 00:30:45,147
Mm.

729
00:30:45,234 --> 00:30:47,236
[cell phone ringing]

730
00:30:47,323 --> 00:30:49,325
It's her.

731
00:30:49,412 --> 00:30:50,413
Hello?

732
00:30:50,500 --> 00:30:52,111
Spoke to my friend.

733
00:30:52,198 --> 00:30:53,808
He wants to meet with you.

734
00:30:53,895 --> 00:30:57,551
2369 Foxglove Parkway..

735
00:30:57,638 --> 00:30:59,727
...Southwest, Las Vegas.

736
00:30:59,814 --> 00:31:01,511
Go there at 3:00 today

737
00:31:01,598 --> 00:31:03,035
and wait for instructions.

738
00:31:03,122 --> 00:31:06,734
2369 Foxglove
Parkway, at 3:00.

739
00:31:06,821 --> 00:31:08,431
Don't forget the gift.

740
00:31:08,518 --> 00:31:10,390
I have it right here.

741
00:31:10,477 --> 00:31:11,652
Don't bring
the whole thing.

742
00:31:11,739 --> 00:31:14,133
Just the head.

743
00:31:15,525 --> 00:31:17,353
Okay.

744
00:31:17,440 --> 00:31:20,313
[inhales deeply]

745
00:31:20,400 --> 00:31:22,881
So you want the good news
or the bad news first?

746
00:31:22,968 --> 00:31:25,144
You lost
two fine agents.

747
00:31:25,231 --> 00:31:27,059
I'm sorry.

748
00:31:27,146 --> 00:31:28,190
Thank you.

749
00:31:28,277 --> 00:31:29,626
I knew Jane
was wrong somehow

750
00:31:29,713 --> 00:31:31,672
but I certainly
never expected this.

751
00:31:31,759 --> 00:31:33,761
Well, nobody did.

752
00:31:33,848 --> 00:31:35,894
We received
no evaluation

753
00:31:35,981 --> 00:31:37,417
that indicated
danger of this sort.

754
00:31:37,504 --> 00:31:39,506
CBI is in no way liable.

755
00:31:39,593 --> 00:31:41,725
Hm.

756
00:31:41,812 --> 00:31:42,901
Well, the question remains.

757
00:31:42,988 --> 00:31:44,990
Why did Jane do this?

758
00:31:45,077 --> 00:31:47,296
Orders from Red John?

759
00:31:47,383 --> 00:31:48,819
If so, why now?

760
00:31:48,907 --> 00:31:50,125
Why Lisbon?

761
00:31:50,212 --> 00:31:51,692
I was talking with Lisbon.

762
00:31:51,779 --> 00:31:53,868
I suggested we...reach out
to try and help Jane

763
00:31:53,955 --> 00:31:56,088
because he was
in trouble and she said "no."

764
00:31:56,175 --> 00:31:57,785
Very firmly.

765
00:31:57,872 --> 00:31:59,743
She said,
"it's not how it looks."

766
00:31:59,830 --> 00:32:01,223
Meaning what?

767
00:32:01,310 --> 00:32:02,529
I don't know.

768
00:32:02,616 --> 00:32:05,271
I don't know
what to think.

769
00:32:05,358 --> 00:32:06,489
[Lisbon]
'Pretty much
the whole neighborhood'

770
00:32:06,576 --> 00:32:07,882
'is in foreclosure.'

771
00:32:07,969 --> 00:32:08,927
'There's hardly anyone there.'

772
00:32:09,014 --> 00:32:10,058
'It's like a ghost town.'

773
00:32:10,145 --> 00:32:11,538
Smart move
by Red John.

774
00:32:11,625 --> 00:32:12,582
Tough to set up
any kind of

775
00:32:12,669 --> 00:32:13,975
'surveillance in advance.'

776
00:32:14,062 --> 00:32:15,455
Any movement's
gonna be conspicuous.

777
00:32:15,542 --> 00:32:16,978
[Rigsby]
He must be suspicious.

778
00:32:17,065 --> 00:32:19,546
No, he's just cautious.

779
00:32:19,633 --> 00:32:21,635
And he's hooked.
He believes.

780
00:32:21,722 --> 00:32:24,029
How can you be sure?

781
00:32:24,116 --> 00:32:27,728
Because he wants
to believe.

782
00:32:27,815 --> 00:32:30,035
We're doing this thing,
so let's just do it.

783
00:32:30,122 --> 00:32:32,559
Is everybody clear on the plan?
We're gonna move soon.

784
00:32:32,646 --> 00:32:33,603
[Rigsby]
'Yeah.'

785
00:32:33,690 --> 00:32:35,475
Hey, you guys, listen..

786
00:32:35,562 --> 00:32:36,737
...I want to apologize

787
00:32:36,824 --> 00:32:37,999
for deceiving you.

788
00:32:38,086 --> 00:32:39,348
Whatever.

789
00:32:39,435 --> 00:32:41,307
And thank you
for...helping me now.

790
00:32:41,394 --> 00:32:43,526
- We're helping the boss.
- Yeah. She's helping you.

791
00:32:43,613 --> 00:32:44,571
We're helping her.

792
00:32:44,658 --> 00:32:46,268
Guys, cut him some slack.

793
00:32:46,355 --> 00:32:48,967
Oh. Yay, team.

794
00:32:49,054 --> 00:32:51,970
[instrumental music]

795
00:32:53,058 --> 00:32:54,015
[engine turns over]

796
00:32:57,018 --> 00:32:58,150
[tires screeching]

797
00:33:02,763 --> 00:33:05,896
A 12. Rigsby W.

798
00:33:05,984 --> 00:33:08,899
[rattling]

799
00:33:12,773 --> 00:33:13,730
[exhales sharply]

800
00:33:13,817 --> 00:33:14,775
No face.

801
00:33:14,862 --> 00:33:15,906
Right.

802
00:33:15,994 --> 00:33:17,473
Could be anybody.

803
00:33:17,560 --> 00:33:18,518
Well, this's
"Rigsby" here.

804
00:33:18,605 --> 00:33:20,999
No mistake.

805
00:33:24,045 --> 00:33:25,655
Do you have
a tape measure?

806
00:33:25,742 --> 00:33:27,179
Sure.

807
00:33:27,266 --> 00:33:29,964
[keypad beeping]

808
00:33:30,051 --> 00:33:32,445
Bill, I need you
to find out ASAP

809
00:33:32,532 --> 00:33:35,622
where Kimball Cho
and Grace Van Pelt are located.

810
00:33:35,709 --> 00:33:36,927
Yeah, right now.

811
00:33:37,015 --> 00:33:38,146
Hold on one second.

812
00:33:38,233 --> 00:33:41,889
Put that
at the top of his head.

813
00:33:43,673 --> 00:33:45,675
5'11".

814
00:33:45,762 --> 00:33:48,461
This isn't Wayne Rigsby.

815
00:33:48,548 --> 00:33:50,985
Yeah. Find out
where they are.

816
00:33:51,072 --> 00:33:52,726
Thanks. And, Bill?

817
00:33:52,813 --> 00:33:54,771
I want arrest warrants
prepped for every single member

818
00:33:54,858 --> 00:33:57,470
of that CBI team,
dead or alive.

819
00:34:00,212 --> 00:34:02,518
[ominous music]

820
00:34:12,659 --> 00:34:15,531
[music continues]

821
00:34:27,935 --> 00:34:30,155
Mm-hm.

822
00:34:30,242 --> 00:34:32,113
The game begins.

823
00:34:32,200 --> 00:34:35,073
[rattling over the radio]

824
00:34:37,466 --> 00:34:40,339
[rattling]

825
00:34:43,516 --> 00:34:44,865
[Patrick over the radio]
'Hey, Lisbon.'

826
00:34:44,952 --> 00:34:46,345
Must have been
a while since you rode on

827
00:34:46,432 --> 00:34:48,390
the handlebars
of a man's bike.

828
00:34:48,477 --> 00:34:49,435
[Lisbon over the radio]
'Ha ha.'

829
00:34:49,522 --> 00:34:51,741
Well, it's kind of romantic.

830
00:34:51,828 --> 00:34:53,569
Wind in your hair.

831
00:34:53,656 --> 00:34:57,225
You're a sick man.

832
00:34:57,312 --> 00:35:00,663
5-0-5-9.

833
00:35:00,750 --> 00:35:04,406
5-0-6-5. 5-0-6..

834
00:35:06,060 --> 00:35:09,803
Uh, there is no 5-0-7-1.

835
00:35:13,154 --> 00:35:15,591
There's nothing.
It's just desert.

836
00:35:15,678 --> 00:35:17,985
There's no one here.

837
00:35:18,072 --> 00:35:19,029
[engine revving distantly]

838
00:35:19,117 --> 00:35:21,031
Hang on.

839
00:35:22,555 --> 00:35:25,123
Long black limousine.

840
00:35:25,210 --> 00:35:26,559
We're moving in,
we'll be on the scene

841
00:35:26,646 --> 00:35:27,647
in three minutes.

842
00:35:27,734 --> 00:35:29,039
Stay healthy till then.

843
00:35:29,127 --> 00:35:30,737
'Wait.'

844
00:35:30,824 --> 00:35:32,695
Let's just be sure.

845
00:35:32,782 --> 00:35:34,436
[car brakes squealing]

846
00:35:39,398 --> 00:35:43,184
[Patrick]
'Large man with a gun..'

847
00:35:43,271 --> 00:35:45,360
'...Red John's girl.
This is it.'

848
00:35:45,447 --> 00:35:47,841
[dramatic music]

849
00:35:47,928 --> 00:35:49,538
All right,
we're moving in.

850
00:35:49,625 --> 00:35:51,758
[tires squealing]

851
00:35:51,845 --> 00:35:53,499
[tires screeching]

852
00:35:55,065 --> 00:35:57,807
FBI. Turn off the car
and show me your hands.

853
00:35:57,894 --> 00:35:59,418
FBI! Nobody move!

854
00:35:59,505 --> 00:36:01,594
CBI! Don't shoot!
We're CBI agents!

855
00:36:01,681 --> 00:36:02,812
You're making
a terrible mistake.

856
00:36:02,899 --> 00:36:04,249
- Get out.
- Now!

857
00:36:04,336 --> 00:36:05,641
We're in the middle
of an operation.

858
00:36:05,728 --> 00:36:07,556
Put your hands
on the car.

859
00:36:07,643 --> 00:36:09,558
[FBI agent #1]
'Stay where you are
and don't move.'

860
00:36:09,645 --> 00:36:11,299
Hi.

861
00:36:11,386 --> 00:36:12,692
Hey.

862
00:36:12,779 --> 00:36:15,477
That the gift?

863
00:36:15,564 --> 00:36:17,610
- Red John in there?
- Mm-hmm.

864
00:36:17,697 --> 00:36:21,962
He's looking forward
to speaking with you.

865
00:36:22,049 --> 00:36:24,007
You know, Patrick..

866
00:36:24,094 --> 00:36:25,879
...there's
a childish hopefulness

867
00:36:25,966 --> 00:36:30,797
about you that is
really quite adorable.

868
00:36:30,884 --> 00:36:33,887
Put it on the hood.

869
00:36:35,976 --> 00:36:38,500
So what is it,
a football?

870
00:36:38,587 --> 00:36:40,589
A cabbage?

871
00:36:41,721 --> 00:36:42,809
Melon..

872
00:36:42,896 --> 00:36:44,724
...honeydew.

873
00:36:44,811 --> 00:36:45,986
Organic.

874
00:36:48,293 --> 00:36:49,424
Adorable.

875
00:36:51,644 --> 00:36:53,385
Frisk him,
then beat him..

876
00:36:53,472 --> 00:36:55,865
...a little.

877
00:36:57,650 --> 00:37:00,522
[instrumental music]

878
00:37:04,918 --> 00:37:06,006
Uh!

879
00:37:06,093 --> 00:37:07,921
Well, well, well.

880
00:37:08,008 --> 00:37:09,618
- Agent, this is a mistake.
- Agent, you don't understand.

881
00:37:09,705 --> 00:37:11,838
- No, I don't understand.
- Please listen to me.

882
00:37:11,925 --> 00:37:13,970
[Darcy]
'You're supposed to
be dead, as are you.'

883
00:37:14,057 --> 00:37:15,537
This is very strange.

884
00:37:15,624 --> 00:37:17,322
Susan, I am begging you.

885
00:37:17,409 --> 00:37:20,238
Please listen
to what I'm saying.

886
00:37:20,325 --> 00:37:21,761
Our fake deaths
were a ruse to trap

887
00:37:21,848 --> 00:37:23,415
Red John,
and it worked.

888
00:37:23,502 --> 00:37:24,677
Jane is with
him right now,

889
00:37:24,764 --> 00:37:26,331
and his life
is in grave danger.

890
00:37:26,418 --> 00:37:29,377
He's at 5-0-7-1
Keston Avenue.

891
00:37:29,464 --> 00:37:30,813
Uh-huh.

892
00:37:30,900 --> 00:37:32,641
That's enough.
We haven't got much time.

893
00:37:32,728 --> 00:37:34,643
Put him
in the passenger seat.

894
00:37:34,730 --> 00:37:35,862
[grunting]

895
00:37:41,607 --> 00:37:42,738
[breathes sharply]

896
00:37:44,827 --> 00:37:46,786
[breathing heavily]

897
00:37:48,178 --> 00:37:50,311
[Red John]
'Hello, Patrick.'

898
00:37:50,398 --> 00:37:53,271
[ominous music]

899
00:37:59,059 --> 00:38:01,148
Hey.

900
00:38:01,235 --> 00:38:02,715
How you doing?

901
00:38:02,802 --> 00:38:05,718
Debonair
at all costs, huh?

902
00:38:05,805 --> 00:38:07,633
When did
you know?

903
00:38:07,720 --> 00:38:09,025
'Oh, you strung me along'

904
00:38:09,112 --> 00:38:10,418
'for a good long while.'

905
00:38:10,505 --> 00:38:12,202
'Well done.'

906
00:38:12,290 --> 00:38:14,292
Luckily, I have
a good friend in the FBI.

907
00:38:14,379 --> 00:38:17,991
So, I found out
when the FBI found out.

908
00:38:19,166 --> 00:38:20,602
Cat got
your tongue?

909
00:38:20,689 --> 00:38:22,648
I have
nothing to say.

910
00:38:22,735 --> 00:38:24,345
Really?

911
00:38:24,432 --> 00:38:26,086
Nothing?

912
00:38:26,173 --> 00:38:28,088
Uh, "go to hell"
goes without saying.

913
00:38:28,175 --> 00:38:30,656
So, yes,
nothing.

914
00:38:30,743 --> 00:38:31,918
As you
well know, Patrick.

915
00:38:32,005 --> 00:38:34,964
There is no hell.

916
00:38:35,051 --> 00:38:38,751
When I die,
I won't be punished.

917
00:38:38,838 --> 00:38:42,450
What if you really
did have a change of heart?

918
00:38:42,537 --> 00:38:45,671
What if you
and I were friends?

919
00:38:45,758 --> 00:38:49,414
[Red John]
'Imagine the life
we could lead.'

920
00:38:49,501 --> 00:38:52,895
It's a higher path,
Patrick.

921
00:38:52,982 --> 00:38:55,594
A nobler existence.

922
00:38:55,681 --> 00:38:58,336
Like I said,
"go to hell."

923
00:38:58,423 --> 00:39:00,642
As you wish.

924
00:39:00,729 --> 00:39:02,775
Lorelei, cut off
two of his fingers.

925
00:39:02,862 --> 00:39:04,167
'You choose which.'

926
00:39:04,254 --> 00:39:05,517
'Then we should go.'

927
00:39:10,783 --> 00:39:11,914
[grunting]

928
00:39:13,176 --> 00:39:14,352
Uh!

929
00:39:16,571 --> 00:39:19,269
- Ah.
- I'm sorry.

930
00:39:19,357 --> 00:39:21,402
Ah! Ah!

931
00:39:21,489 --> 00:39:24,362
[siren wailing]

932
00:39:25,972 --> 00:39:27,147
[gunfire]

933
00:39:29,236 --> 00:39:32,152
[dramatic music]

934
00:39:35,068 --> 00:39:38,027
[siren wailing]

935
00:39:38,114 --> 00:39:39,725
[tires screeching]

936
00:39:39,812 --> 00:39:42,684
[siren wailing]

937
00:39:46,122 --> 00:39:49,038
[gun firing]

938
00:39:52,128 --> 00:39:54,914
[gun firing continues]

939
00:39:58,396 --> 00:40:01,311
[instrumental music]

940
00:40:02,791 --> 00:40:06,142
- FBI!
- FBI, turn off the vehicle!

941
00:40:07,753 --> 00:40:08,797
[FBI agent #2]
'Let me see your hands.'

942
00:40:08,884 --> 00:40:10,712
C'mon, outta the car.

943
00:40:10,799 --> 00:40:13,019
Get your hands up.

944
00:40:13,106 --> 00:40:15,282
Turn around,
face the car.

945
00:40:15,369 --> 00:40:18,285
[instrumental music]

946
00:40:22,985 --> 00:40:24,596
[beeping on the speakers]

947
00:40:24,683 --> 00:40:26,902
[woman on the speaker]
'This call
has been disconnected.'

948
00:40:26,989 --> 00:40:29,122
'Please hang up
and try your call again.'

949
00:40:29,209 --> 00:40:30,123
[beeping on the speakers]

950
00:40:30,210 --> 00:40:31,298
Oh, shit!

951
00:40:31,385 --> 00:40:32,691
'This call
has been disconnected.'

952
00:40:32,778 --> 00:40:33,779
Ugh!

953
00:40:36,477 --> 00:40:37,609
Uh!

954
00:40:40,873 --> 00:40:42,048
Ah.

955
00:40:44,050 --> 00:40:45,225
[car door opens]

956
00:40:45,312 --> 00:40:46,444
[car doors closes]

957
00:40:52,145 --> 00:40:53,407
You all right?

958
00:40:53,494 --> 00:40:55,714
Yeah, I'm fine.

959
00:40:55,801 --> 00:40:58,368
Never better.

960
00:40:58,456 --> 00:41:01,371
[instrumental music]

961
00:41:01,459 --> 00:41:03,199
[siren wailing in distance]

962
00:41:03,286 --> 00:41:06,202
[siren wailing]

963
00:41:08,422 --> 00:41:11,338
[instrumental music]

964
00:41:17,257 --> 00:41:19,868
I'm very happy
to meet you, Lorelei.

965
00:41:19,955 --> 00:41:21,522
We rarely get
the chance to talk

966
00:41:21,609 --> 00:41:24,525
to someone who knows
Red John so well.

967
00:41:24,612 --> 00:41:26,484
Good to meet you, too.

968
00:41:26,571 --> 00:41:29,748
Heard so much about you.

969
00:41:32,315 --> 00:41:35,188
We were lovers,
him and me.

970
00:41:35,275 --> 00:41:38,626
Did he tell you that?

971
00:41:38,713 --> 00:41:41,455
No?

972
00:41:41,542 --> 00:41:43,805
Why not, lover?

973
00:41:43,892 --> 00:41:46,460
[Lorelei]
'You ashamed of me?'

974
00:41:46,547 --> 00:41:50,072
Did we do something bad?

975
00:41:50,159 --> 00:41:51,509
I know it's hard
to believe now

976
00:41:51,596 --> 00:41:54,642
but you're
gonna talk to us.

977
00:41:54,729 --> 00:41:56,601
[Patrick]
'You're gonna break down,
and you're gonna tell us'

978
00:41:56,688 --> 00:41:57,993
everything you know
about Red John.

979
00:41:58,080 --> 00:42:01,606
You're gonna
sing like a bird.

980
00:42:01,693 --> 00:42:03,390
No, lover.

981
00:42:03,477 --> 00:42:05,914
I won't.

982
00:42:06,001 --> 00:42:08,221
Yes, you will.

983
00:42:08,308 --> 00:42:10,266
Yes, you will.

984
00:42:10,353 --> 00:42:13,269
[instrumental music]

985
00:42:27,893 --> 00:42:29,590
[theme music]

986
00:42:40,253 --> 00:42:43,125
[music continues]

